    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, labelled `FY<YY>` by its **ending** calendar year \u2014 e.g. 2026-07-01 \u2192 `FY27`, 2026-06-30 \u2192 `FY26`), all derived from the already-business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`) to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it. Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `fiscalYear(owner)` read-time derivation mapped onto `OwnerDto.fiscalYear`, plus a private `fiscalYearOf(date)` helper. Returns `null` (field omitted) when there's no registration date.\n\n3. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 The `-M<YY>` year segment now uses the fiscal year of the registration date rather than the calendar year.\n\n4. **`AssignMembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 Tenure is now counted in **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearOf(now) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate)`) instead of 365-day windows; the +3 tenure bonus applies when more than one fiscal year has elapsed. Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit`/`TENURE_DAYS_FOR_POINTS`.\n\nThe new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test passes (verified `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`), and the full suite of 263 tests remains green. Since tests create owners dated ~today, the tenure change is behaviour-preserving for them (0 elapsed years either way), while the fiscal-year membership-number segment is correctly exercised (`...-M27` for an August 2026 registration).",
